  "body": "## What\n\nDesign record for #6048: `doc/2026-11-08T20-45-40Z_design_atlas_presidio_ner.md` — the Atlas Presidio NER pass design under parent #6021.\n\nDecides, per the #6048 acceptance criteria:\n\n- **Recognizer set** — Tier A (checksum/structure-backed: cards/Luhn, IBAN/mod-97, US SSN/ITIN/bank/passport/licence, UK NHS; IBAN global) vs Tier B (NER + context: PERSON/ORG/LOCATION, pattern-only recognizers), with a two-signal emission rule for Tier B candidates. Country recognizers beyond US/UK are OFF by default, provenance-gated, per the #6048 finding on FP risk absent context.\n- **Tier scoping** — full Tier A+B pass over the internal tier (107,001 chunks, cited from #6021); Tier A 100% + Tier B 25% stratified sample (160 of 638 chunks, seeded) over the secret tier for calibration, with an explicit escalation rule to 100% per source class.\n- **Cost** — planning model with labelled estimates: ~1–3 h off-peak wall-clock for the internal census on the fleet laptop; mandatory 1,000-chunk pilot to measure throughput and candidate rate before any census; reviewer-load ceiling as the real budget.\n- **Batching/checkpointing** — 500-chunk batches per shard, run manifest keyed by recognizer config hash + model versions, idempotent resume.\n- **FP review queue** — quarantine candidates only; tier-lock upward on confirm; never silent delete; recognizer + context attached; findings handled at secret-tier sensitivity.\n- **Rejected alternatives** (NER everywhere, no NER, full secret pass, all country recognizers, auto-quarantine, hosted PII API), **invariants**, and an explicit **§8 fork check: nothing in this record changes a #6021 scanner-design decision**.\n\nSource note: the prior-art path named in the #6048 body is absent on the fleet laptop; the record is written from the finding summary in the #6048 body and says so, per the task packet.\n\n## Tests\n\nDocs-only. `git diff --check` clean; file sha256 verified identical between authoring copy and worktree. No code tests apply (per packet).\n\nQueue task 13549 (lane code-v, direct).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796762957&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7809&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7809&signature=c8b6a48f7a540b7776f27d695bf9c7f3b2db72e823fcf0bb8af8ceae28357100\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7809?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
